<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="JirAI: FAQ and known limitations" id="JirAI-FAQ">

    <primary-label ref="jirai"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Answers to common questions about JirAI, troubleshooting tips and the known limitations.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Common questions, troubleshooting tips and known limitations.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Answers about JirAI for Jira Cloud in JetBrains IDEs: licensing, the 365-day issue list, agent tools, read-only descriptions and known limitations.</web-summary>

    <chapter title="General questions" id="general-questions">
        <deflist>
            <def title="Does JirAI support Jira Server or Jira Data Center?">
                <p>No. JirAI works with Jira Cloud only.</p>
                <p>Jira Server and Jira Data Center use a different API and sign-in model.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="How does the free trial work?">
                <p>JirAI is a paid plugin with a 7-day free trial.</p>
                <p>Start the trial or activate a license in <ui-path>Help | Register</ui-path>.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Installation.topic" anchor="licensing-and-trial">Licensing and free trial</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Does JirAI collect telemetry or send my code anywhere?">
                <p>No. JirAI has no telemetry or analytics, and it does not read or send your source code.</p>
                <p>Requests with your credentials go only to the Jira site you signed in to.</p>
                <p>Markdown documents are sent to Jira only when you push them.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Why does the issue list show only issues from the last 365 days?">
                <p>Every search and filter in the issue list covers issues created in the last 365 days.</p>
                <p>To open an older issue, type its key, for example <code>DEMO-123</code>, in the search field.</p>
                <p>See <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" anchor="search-and-sort">Search and sort</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Can I connect to several Jira sites?">
                <p>No. JirAI connects to one Jira Cloud site at a time; signing in to another site replaces the current one.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Can I see delivery metrics such as cycle time?">
                <p>Yes. Open a space with <control>Space Summary</control> and use the <control>Reports</control> tab.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Metrics.topic">Space summary, list and reports</a>.</p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Troubleshooting" id="troubleshooting-questions">
        <deflist>
            <def title="Why is the issue list empty after I sign in?">
                <p>The list starts with the <control>Assigned to Me</control> quick filter and shows only issues created in the last 365 days.</p>
                <p>When nothing matches, it reads <control>Nothing matches the filters.</control>; choose <control>All Issues</control> in the <control>Filters</control> menu, or click <control>Clear filters</control>.</p>
                <p>See <a href="Work-with-Jira-Issues.topic" anchor="filters">Filter the list</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="My AI assistant does not see the JirAI tools. Why?">
                <p>The tools need the IDE's MCP server, which is off by default.</p>
                <p>Turn it on in <ui-path>Settings | Tools | MCP Server</ui-path>, configure your assistant with <control>Auto-Configure</control> and check <control>Exposed Tools</control>.</p>
                <p>The IDE must be running with a project open.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Agent-Tools.topic" anchor="enable-agent-tools">Turn on the agent tools</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Why can't I edit a description?">
                <p>The description contains content that has no Markdown equivalent, such as a table, a panel or an image.</p>
                <p>Saving it from the IDE would lose that content, so JirAI shows the reason and an <control>Open in browser</control> link.</p>
                <p>See <a href="Jira-Timeline-and-Description-Editor.topic" anchor="description-readonly">Descriptions you can edit only in Jira</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Why is a board marked Limited?">
                <p>It is a team-managed board.</p>
                <p>Team-managed boards do not open in the IDE; choosing one opens it in Jira.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Why does my Scrum board show only some of its sprints?">
                <p>The <control>Board</control> tab shows a Scrum board's active sprint.</p>
                <p>When a board has more than one active sprint, it shows the first and names the others in a notice.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="JirAI says I am not signed in, or that the sign-in was rejected. What do I do?">
                <p>JirAI shows <control>Not signed in to Jira, or the sign-in was rejected.</control> when Jira no longer accepts your API token, for example because the token expired or was revoked.</p>
                <p>Create a new API token, choose <control>Sign Out</control> in the options menu (<control>⋮</control>) of the <control>JirAI</control> tool window, and sign in again.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Sign-In-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="switch-site-or-token">Switch sites or replace the API token</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Where is my API token stored?">
                <p>In the IDE credential store, which is the operating system keychain or the IDE's KeePass file.</p>
                <p>Under Remote Development, it is stored on the host.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Sign-In-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="credential-storage">Where JirAI stores credentials</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="How do I use JirAI behind a corporate proxy?">
                <p>JirAI uses the proxy in <ui-path>Settings | Appearance &amp; Behavior | System Settings | HTTP Proxy</ui-path>.</p>
                <p>SOCKS proxies are not supported: with a SOCKS proxy set, JirAI connects to Jira directly.</p>
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Sign-In-and-Configuration.topic" anchor="corporate-proxy">Use JirAI behind a corporate proxy</a>.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="How do I report a problem?">
                <p>See <a href="JirAI-Reference-and-Support.topic">Support</a> for where to report it and what to include.</p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Known limitations" id="known-limitations">
        <list>
            <li><p>Jira Cloud only, with one site at a time.</p></li>
            <li><p>Sign-in with an API token only; OAuth is not supported.</p></li>
            <li><p>Issue list searches cover issues created in the last 365 days, except a search for a single issue key.</p></li>
            <li><p>No JQL: queries are built from the filters and the search field.</p></li>
            <li><p>Existing comments cannot be edited, only added and deleted.</p></li>
            <li><p>Descriptions with tables, panels, media and similar content can be edited only in Jira.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Breakdown</control> lists direct children only.</p></li>
            <li><p>On a board, cards move through the card menu only; team-managed boards open in Jira.</p></li>
            <li><p>The <control>Timeline</control> tab of a space opens the space in Jira.</p></li>
            <li><p>There is no branch-from-issue or other version control integration.</p></li>
            <li><p>In the details tab, custom fields, the reporter and the issue type are read-only.</p></li>
            <li><p>Board cards do not open the issue details in the IDE.</p></li>
            <li><p><control>Push to Jira</control> works only on files with the <path>.md</path> extension.</p></li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

